parts.stem:
A student takes a torch apart. Inside there are three cells in a row, a metal spring and metal strips, a switch, a lamp and a plastic case.
Explain how the torch works as an electric circuit.
Your answer should include:
• why the cells must all face the same way;
• which parts conduct, which part insulates, and why;
• what the switch does;
• the direction of the electron flow and of the conventional current.
This question also assesses the quality of your written communication, including your use of specialist scientific terms.
